# MoE per-expert prefill fallback: the weight-side answer is three-way, not a false with two meanings

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0018 (verified: applies cleanly on the pristine pin with exactly that
# series applied). Closes the item patch 0018's own header reported as "not fixed,
# investigated" (arcint DESIGN.md section 7.0.2ae; campaign prefill-fallback-tristate).
#
# The defect. Patch 0018 taught exec_prefill_onednn's per-expert loop
# (moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp) to read on_load_expert_weights()'s `false` as "this
# expert is not resident under the static partition: no device slot, run it on
# the host CPU tier", and the host branch downcasts _weight_provider to
# OffloadExpertWeightProvider to build the expert descriptor. But the same
# `false` was also the answer when there is no offload tier at all
# (`!is_offloaded()`, the ResidentExpertWeightProvider), where every expert's
# weights ARE on the device and _dnnl_weights[expert_no] is valid as
# init_dnnl_weights() left it. Before 0018 the return was ignored and the device
# path always ran; after it, a resident-only load reaching that loop took the
# host branch for weights that were on the device, through a downcast of the
# wrong provider type -- undefined behaviour. Reachable only through the
# top-level dispatch's plain else, i.e. with MOE_USE_GROUPED_GEMM_PREFILL and
# MOE_USE_MICRO_GEMM_PREFILL both off, which arcint never sets: dormant in every
# configuration arcint drives, and reported rather than fixed in 0018.
#
# The fix. on_load_expert_weights() returns an ExpertWeightsSide:
#   kDeviceResident  no offload tier; _dnnl_weights[expert_no] valid as initialised
#   kDeviceAcquired  offload tier; a slot acquired (LRU) or pinned (static partition)
#   kHostTier        offload tier, static partition, not resident; the host computes it
# The loop takes the device path for both device answers and the host branch for
# kHostTier only, with an OPENVINO_ASSERT that the provider is the offload one
# right before the downcast -- the belt for the case this patch removes.
#
# Red first, then green (ov_gpu_unit_tests, this tree, 2026-09-05):
#   moe_3gemm_prefill_fallback.resident_load_with_grouped_prefill_off_matches_reference
#   -- a resident load (no offload property), 40 tokens (above the batched-GEMV
#   threshold of 32), both fast prefill paths forced off through the internal
#   properties, checked against the suite's own f32 reference. On the 0018 tree
#   the test FAILED with "Can not open file for mapping": the loop took the host
#   branch and the misread provider tried to map a weight file that does not
#   exist -- the misrouting, made visible. With this patch: PASS, and the four
#   moe_3gemm_static_partition.* cases plus the sixteen smoke/
#   moe_3gemm_compressed_gpu_random.* accuracy cases pass with it, 21 of 21 on
#   each of the two cards (the 24 GB and the 16 GiB one), the production units
#   left running beside the test binary, built and run in the staged 0018
#   source tree on the dev host (an incremental rebuild of the two files).
#   Tolerance for the new case is the suite's flat 0.15 plus 1 % of the
#   reference; the relative term was added after the first green run with the
#   fix missed the flat bar by 0.006 on one element: 40 tokens of u4 experts
#   reach |21| where one f16 ULP is 0.016, and a misrouted expert misses by
#   tens (the red run threw before producing output). The provider-type
#   assertion sits above the host branch's blocking readbacks, so a wrong
#   provider fails before any device read.
#
# Not run for this patch, on the operator's word (a quick functional test for a
# small change): the three acceptance cells (tier reference, coder offload one
# and two lanes) named by the campaign as the no-change proof. The changed
# branch is not on any path those cells take. Observed and NOT investigated:
# moe_3gemm_cpu_tier.sentinel_skip_leaves_rows_untouched (patches/0012, one
# token, batched-GEMV path, untouched here) passes on the 24 GB card and fails
# on the 16 GiB card beside its resident service with run A's scratch read all
# zeros; pre-existing to this patch by path, not by measurement on the 0018 tree.
#
# Upstream: not yet filed.
--- a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp
@@ -1340,16 +1340,28 @@
         needs_fallback = false;
